{"id": "rijks-200108249", "status": "ok", "meta": "Michiel de Ruyter leans on a globe with a baton in hand in Ferdinand Bol's 1667 portrait, painted after the victory of 1666.", "about": "Michiel de Ruyter stands before an open curtain, his right arm on a globe and a commander's baton in his hand. A seascape behind the balustrade shows his flagship, the Zeven Provinciën. He wears the French Order of Saint Michael. A map on the table shows the coast of Zeeland and Flanders with Walcheren in the middle, the island where he was born. Ferdinand Bol signed and dated it 1667. It marks the victory of the Four Days' Battle in 1666, after which portraits of the admiral were to hang in every admiralty council room.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-44--93893a10127f52e6cf3132ee3c9491b8", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-44--93893a10127f52e6cf3132ee3c9491b8", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/200108249"], "check": "clean"}
{"id": "rijks-200109297", "status": "ok", "meta": "Ernest de Beveren, lord of West-IJsselmonde and De Lindt, in Aert de Gelder's 1685 portrait, later sold for Hitler's planned museum in Linz.", "about": "Ernest de Beveren, lord of West-IJsselmonde and De Lindt, stands at a table and gestures with his right hand. He served Dordrecht as alderman and mayor, and later as its postmaster. Aert de Gelder signed and dated the portrait in 1685. In 1942 its owner, Jean Joseph Marie Chabot, sold it with two other paintings to the Dienststelle Mühlmann, which bought them for Hitler's planned Führermuseum in Linz. It was recovered after the war, in 1945.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-3969--5c4ed4650cb22dcd604123d6e245d3dd", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-3969--5c4ed4650cb22dcd604123d6e245d3dd", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/200109297"], "check": "clean"}
{"id": "rijks-200109333", "status": "ok", "meta": "Adriaan Valckenier, governor-general of the Dutch East Indies, in Theodorus Justinus Rheen's portrait of 1737, ordered by the sitter.", "about": "Adriaan Valckenier stands half-length with a commander's baton in his right hand, his left arm resting on a book that carries the VOC monogram. The arms of his family, the Dutch East Indies, the Republic and Batavia fill the corners, and a ship sails behind him. He was governor-general of the Dutch East Indies. The portrait belongs to a series of governors-general, and Valckenier ordered it himself. Theodorus Justinus Rheen signed it in 1737. It moved from the Landvoogd-Galerij at Weltevreden, Jakarta, to the museum in 1950.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-3778--83f086cea7d1fab261de14180b1be4ba", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/SK-A-3778--83f086cea7d1fab261de14180b1be4ba", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/200109333"], "check": "clean"}
