{"id": "rijks-200120542", "status": "ok", "meta": "Judith and her maid carry off the head of Holofernes in Georg Pencz's 1539 print, held by the Rijksmuseum.", "about": "Judith and her maid walk away with the head of Holofernes on a platter, leaving his headless body on a bed. Georg Pencz made the print in 1539, and the Rijksmuseum holds it.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/RP-P-OB-10.983--53daa7913bb06abdd3871685b27bed4d", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/RP-P-OB-10.983--53daa7913bb06abdd3871685b27bed4d", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/200120542"], "check": "clean"}
{"id": "rijks-200121511", "status": "ok", "meta": "Wenceslaus Hollar's 1673 print of a round Roman building, one of two prints of Roman ruins in the Rijksmuseum.", "about": "Wenceslaus Hollar made this print of a round Roman building in 1673. It is one of two prints in a series of Roman ruins. The Rijksmuseum bought it with support from the F.G. Waller-Fonds.", "museum_record": "https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/RP-P-1963-28--c3370d708394e947e5b417ca65dfb1ee", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/nl/collectie/object/RP-P-1963-28--c3370d708394e947e5b417ca65dfb1ee", "https://id.rijksmuseum.nl/200121511"], "check": "clean"}
